{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100907","id":2254658893,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6GY11N","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100907","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100907.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100907.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100907","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100907/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100907/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100907/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/82b97314119fa8f656ae5000a2ab65701f905a2d","number":100907,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Store view depth instead of ray length in occlusion buffer","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This has two advantages :\n- Trades buffer update performance (constant time per frame) for geometry culling performance (linear time with the number of objects). Considering Occlusion Culling is primarily designed for large scenes, this should have a small positive impact\n- Removes the need for calling `length()` on the geometry position vector (Z coordinate is used instead) which avoids overflows with very far away objects (> ~1e19m in single precision) and makes Occlusion Culling suitable for large scenes\n\nThis may also allow removing orthogonal vs perspective code paths during culling (to be investigated)","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2024-12-29T17:04:07Z","updated_at":"2025-05-09T09:09:17Z","closed_at":"2025-02-27T15:03:55Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"2a45fde82da1849f460bf33c29ca583f187d1ced","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Flarkk:occlusion_z_buffer","ref":"occlusion_z_buffer","repo":{"id":391085606,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkzOTEwODU2MDY=","name":"godot","full_name":"Flarkk/godot","owner":{"login":"Flarkk","id":496